o his  citizens there was nothing left to do  to let you play out your little scenario  finnick had  absolutely no choice in the matter snow  threatened to harm  all of his loved ones if he didn't obey  his orders  this is where his facade comes in he  puts on a show for everyone around him  so they don't suspect what's really  going on behind the scenes  but finnick did get something out of it  in the long run  instead of getting paid cash by the  capital people he asked for secrets  this background knowledge actually makes  his introduction to katniss make more  sense remember when she asks him  well then how do people pay for the  pleasure of your company with secrets  that's what he was referring to those  secrets  gave the resistance a huge piece of info  later on  finnick knew how snow had kept his power  for so long  snow was poisoning anyone who got in his  way while also  masking his crime by drinking the poison  along with them  he had all the antidotes of course but  the poison  left irreversible damage and that's why  he wears roses  to mask the smell of the sores in his  mouth we know  tmi it's also why he meets his demise  even though katniss changes her bow's  aim to coin  if phenix character is finally starting  to make sense after hearing his  backstory  you're not alone the film gave us pieces  of his character but never the whole  picture  we never truly got to grasp who he was  apart from being a victor  turns out his story might just be the  most interesting one in the film  his backstory of becoming a victor isn't  even the tip of the iceberg when it  comes to things they left out about him  the more people on our side the closer  we are to peter and annie  annie the love of phoenix life we do get  a few scenes with her  and a brief introduction but it's safe  to say the filmmakers paid her  basically no attention which is bizarre  because  she's not only important to finnick but  katniss and peeta as well  annie was introduced later on in the 